      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many labels. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nCould this be a typo? These are some common regimens:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking it with pharmacy or your attending first."
      }
     ],
